tls: always refresh the queue when reading sock

[ Backport of upstream commit 4ab26bce3969f8fd925fe6f6f551e4d1a508c68b
  ("tls: always refresh the queue when reading sock");
  landed in fbk as c76f6f437c46. Absent from 6.11-fbk10 (crash kernel). ]

TCP can compact / collapse the skbs in the receive queue (fast-path skb
compaction, or tcp_collapse under memory pressure) between two
->data_ready() invocations. TLS caches a snapshot of that queue in the
strparser anchor's frag_list the first time it parses a record header.

tls_strp_read_sock() only reloaded that snapshot inside the
"if (!strp->stm.full_len)" block, i.e. only when it had *not* yet parsed
the record length. When the record header was parsed on an earlier call
but the full record had not arrived yet (inq < full_len -> partial read,
early return), a later call with inq >= full_len skipped the reload and
handed a STALE frag_list (and stale stm.offset) to
tls_strp_check_queue_ok(). If the head skb of that stale snapshot had
since been freed/merged, the "while (skb->len < len) { skb = skb->next; }"
walk runs off a freed/short chain and dereferences a NULL skb->next:

    BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000028
    RIP: tls_strp_check_rcv+0x109/0x230 [tls]   (tls_strp_check_queue_ok)
    tls_data_ready -> tcp_data_queue -> tcp_rcv_established -> tcp_v6_rcv

(0x28 = offsetof(struct sk_buff, cb) + offsetof(struct tcp_skb_cb, seq),
 i.e. TCP_SKB_CB(NULL)->seq.)

Upstream observed the same stack as a KASAN slab-use-after-free; without
KASAN the freed/reused skb yields a NULL ->next and an oops.

Always reload the queue before checking it. The fast path is to have the
record in the queue when we wake anyway (the path going down
"if !strp->stm.full_len"), so this adds no meaningful cost.

Fixes: 0d87bbd39d7f ("tls: strp: make sure the TCP skbs do not have overlapping data")
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
---
 net/tls/tls_strp.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/tls/tls_strp.c b/net/tls/tls_strp.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/net/tls/tls_strp.c
+++ b/net/tls/tls_strp.c
@@ -511,9 +511,8 @@ static int tls_strp_read_sock(struct tls_strparser *strp)
 	if (inq < strp->stm.full_len)
 		return tls_strp_read_copy(strp, true);

+	tls_strp_load_anchor_with_queue(strp, inq);
 	if (!strp->stm.full_len) {
-		tls_strp_load_anchor_with_queue(strp, inq);
-
 		sz = tls_rx_msg_size(strp, strp->anchor);
 		if (sz < 0) {
 			tls_strp_abort_strp(strp, sz);
